{
  "id": "supermarket",
  "title": "At the supermarket",
  "titleNl": "In de supermarkt",
  "level": "A1",
  "intro": "The questions at the till come fast and in almost the same order every time. Learn to recognise them and you can answer without switching to English.",
  "notes": [
    {
      "title": "u or je?",
      "body": [
        "Shop staff usually say u, the polite “you”, to adults. Younger staff often say je. You can answer either way and nobody will mind."
      ],
      "examples": [
        { "nl": "[Wilt u] een tasje?", "en": "Would you like a bag? (polite)" },
        { "nl": "[Wil je] een tasje?", "en": "Would you like a bag? (informal)" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Weights at the counter: ons and pond",
      "body": [
        "At the cheese or meat counter, people still use old units. One ons is 100 grams. One pond is 500 grams."
      ],
      "examples": [
        { "nl": "[Twee ons] jonge kaas, graag.", "en": "200 grams of young cheese, please." },
        { "nl": "[Een pond] gehakt, graag.", "en": "500 grams of mince, please." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "cards": [
